"Absolutexistence, a being beyond this world's gods, brought Nala here."
"It fishes other worlds for minds that might mend this world's rot, and Nala is its newest cast."
"The rot it wants mended is the black filth under the world, the root of curse power."
"The one it cast before went across the sea, and the filth under these lands is still unmended."
"It took the one before into a dead boy's body; Alan it took whole, asleep, body and clothes."
"It remade Alan's body for this world, patterned on the heroine of the book open on his knee."
"It counted all that touched his skin as part of him, so the shirt and tights came; the book fell."
"It gave her the common tongue and its script in the remaking, and nothing more."
"It gave her no mana, no skill and no word; it watches to see what path she finds."
"It set her far from the one it cast before, beside a road with rubbish in its ditch."
"Her body is a mortal's, whole and healthy, with no scar, no callus and no other life's marks."
"Her core is unformed, and she can wake to mana as any mortal can."
"No sense a mage has marks her as from elsewhere; only her words, ways and clothes do."
"Her mind keeps all Alan knew, and if she reads in earnest, Speed Reading counts from 15."
"The System shows her nothing until she wakes to mana, then shows every skill she has earned."
"The being does not answer calls, and spoke to the one before only once, through a screen."
"Her path, if she finds one, grows from something Alan loved, as trash was the other's."
"Cloth like her tights is woven nowhere here; a clothier or a fashion mage would pay gold for it."
"Her shirt's fine even knit outdoes any mortal loom here; a ragman would give a silver for it."
